#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:132
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: a person may have a picture of the whole page kept, sent by their browser extension or drawn here from the kept source with scripts and the network off. A picture taken in somebody's browser shows the page as they were seeing it, signed in or not. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep one."
msgstr ""
"Jah: inimesel võib olla säilitatud pilt kogu lehest, mille saatis tema brauserilaiend või mis joonistati siin säilitatud allikast, skriptid ja võrk välja lülitatud. Kellegi brauseris tehtud pilt näitab lehte nii, nagu ta seda nägi, sisse logitud või mitte. Ei või seadmata: kellegi püüdmised seda ei säilita."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:123
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: a person may have the page's source kept beside what was read from it, exactly as it was parsed, so that a capture can be checked against it and read again by a better parser. It is kept as text and never shown as a page. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep it, whatever they have chosen."
msgstr ""
"Jah: inimesel võib olla lehe allikas säilitatud sellest loetu kõrval, täpselt nii, nagu see parsiti, et püüdmist saaks selle vastu kontrollida ja parem parser saaks selle uuesti lugeda. See säilitatakse tekstina ja seda ei näidata kunagi lehena. Ei või seadmata: kellegi püüdmised seda ei säilita, olenemata sellest, mida nad on valinud."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:70
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: anyone who finds the address may create an account. No: invitation only. An empty instance always offers the sign-up form, so somebody can become the first account."
msgstr ""
"Jah: igaüks, kes aadressi leiab, tohib konto luua. Ei: ainult kutsega. Tühi eksemplar pakub alati registreerimisvormi, et keegi saaks esimeseks kontoks."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:79
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: somebody who arrives through the identity provider is signed straight in, without being asked for a code as well. Say yes only if you know that provider checks identity at least as carefully as Postulo would. It never applies to a password sign-in, and it removes nobody's authenticator app. A passkey already counts on its own and needs no setting."
msgstr ""
"Jah: kes tuleb identiteedipakkuja kaudu, logitakse otse sisse, ilma et küsitaks ka koodi. Vastake jah üksnes siis, kui teate, et see pakkuja kontrollib isikusamasust vähemalt sama hoolikalt kui Postulo. See ei kehti kunagi parooliga sisselogimise kohta ega eemalda kelleltki autentimisrakendust. Pääsuvõti loeb juba iseseisvalt ega vaja seadet."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py:90
#, draft
msgid ""
"Yes: somebody who has forgotten their password can ask for a code at their primary address and type it back. A code rather than a link, because mail scanners follow links and would spend one before the person read it. It is never a second factor: an authenticator app is still asked for. Offered only while this instance's mail is actually getting through."
msgstr ""
"Jah: kes on oma parooli unustanud, saab küsida koodi oma peamisele aadressile ja selle tagasi sisestada. Kood, mitte link, sest postiskannerid järgivad linke ja kulutaksid selle ära enne, kui inimene selle läbi loeb. See ei ole kunagi teine tegur: autentimisrakendust küsitakse ikka. Pakutakse ainult seni, kuni selle instantsi post tegelikult kohale jõuab."

